me scores to guesses and returns the absolute difference for each match.\n    A value of 0 indicates a correct guess.\"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for score, single_guess in zip(game, guess):\n        if score == single_guess:\n            results.append(0)\n        else:\n            results.append(abs(score - single_guess))\n    return results", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/153": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "def Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the strongest extension based on the difference between uppercase and lowercase\n    letters in its name, and returns a formatted string: ClassName.StrongestExtensionName.\n    In case of ties in strength, the extension appearing first in the list is chosen.\n    \"\"\"\n    def compute_strength(name: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the strength of an extension name (CAP - SM).\"\"\"\n        cap = sum(1 for char in name if char.isupper())\n        sm = sum(1 for char in name if char.islower())\n        return cap - sm\n\n    if not extensions:\n        return \"\" # Or handle error, but design context implies non-empty list.\n\n    strongest_extension_name = max(extensions, key=compute_strength)\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_extension_name}\"", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/155": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/155", "solution": "import math\ndef even_odd_count(num):\n    \"\"\"Given an integer. return a tuple that has the number of even and odd digits respectively.\"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n    # Use absolute value to ignore the sign\n    s_num = str(abs(num))\n\n    for digit_char in s_num:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if digit % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return (even_count, odd_count)", "base_status": "pass", 